0.2929L5.29289 9.29289C5.68341 8.90236 6.31658 8.90236 6.7071 9.29289Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></button></h2>
<p>To consume Codex output in scripts, use JSON Lines output:</p>
<pre class="astro-code astro-code-themes github-light github-dark" style="background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;overflow-x:auto" tabindex="0" data-language="bash"><code><span class="line"><span style="color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0">codex</span><span style="color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF"> exec</span><span style="color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF"> --json</span><span style="color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF"> &quot;summarize the repo structure&quot;</span><span style="color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583"> |</span><span style="color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0"> jq</span></span></code></pre>
<p>When you enable <code>--json</code>, <code>stdout</code> becomes a JSON Lines (JSONL) stream so you can capture every event Codex emits while it’s running. Event types include <code>thread.started</code>, <code>turn.started</code>, <code>turn.completed</code>, <code>turn.failed</code>, <code>item.*</code>, and <code>error</code>.</p>
--
