<p>If you omit the prompt argument, Codex reads the prompt from stdin. Use <code>codex exec -</code> when you want to force that behavior explicitly.</p>
<p>The <code>-</code> sentinel is useful when another command or script is generating the entire prompt dynamically. This is a good fit when you store prompts in files, assemble prompts with shell scripts, or combine live command output with instructions before handing the whole prompt to Codex.</p>
